{
  "id": "pilot01-evidence",
  "title_zh": "讨论调查结果",
  "context_zh": "同事避免将相关性误说成因果关系。",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s01",
      "speaker": "Nora",
      "text": "The survey suggests that people who cycle to work feel less stressed."
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s02",
      "speaker": "Sam",
      "text": "What evidence supports that conclusion? How large was the sample?"
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s03",
      "speaker": "Nora",
      "text": "Only forty people replied. That is a limitation."
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s04",
      "speaker": "Sam",
      "text": "Then we should not assume that cycling caused the difference."
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s05",
      "speaker": "Nora",
      "text": "Right. We can describe the pattern, but we need further research."
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot01-evidence-s06",
      "speaker": "Sam",
      "text": "Let us include that distinction in the report so the claim is accurate."
    }
  ],
